  "details": "You can check it in Monument world. It appears the lower/body part of the tower has custom layer and it's not part of Unity / VRChat standard layers.\n\nBecause custom added layers might not visible in Photo output (the saved image if you make screenshot/photo of the scene)\n\nWhat makes it even more weird, the stream output showed everything fine, also in VR side (OpenVR stream) everything is visible.\n\nThis is not only problem. Also worlds with ray-marched effect in background, the generated content, has special layer, made it invisible on photo side. You can not make photos from it. I didn't know about it.\n\nI just post it as a bug, because it is confusing for people who make photos even they can see it fine on camera. IMHO photo output should equal to stream output to avoid confusion otherwise i will post it as sort of bug.\n\nPeople are not happy because they don't know about this problem with \"failed\" photos without tower on it. Not great!\n\nBut first, why is tower not visible on the photo output? This is less great because there are people who want make photos of the big tower - but it's not possible. They're forced to record it with stream output side. Or smash PrintScreen button. Not sure if F12 works for desktop....\n\nCan you do something about this? Make stream output = photo output? Or is there a reason it's not possible?\n\nMight affect Quest side too, but ray-marched part don't work on Quest. But Mountain has quest side.",
